FIPS 180-4 ("Secure Hash Standard (SHS)", NIST, 2015)
https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/FIPS/NIST.FIPS.180-4.pdf

  sello's `src/sello/private/sha512.nim` (in-house SHA-512, RFC-006) is
  implemented directly from FIPS 180-4 Section 5 (preprocessing/padding)
  and Section 6.4 (the SHA-512 message schedule and compression
  function). The eighty `K` round constants and the eight `Sha512IV`
  words are transcribed verbatim from the spec's own published hex
  tables (FIPS 180-4 SS4.2.3 / SS5.3.5). FIPS 180-4 is a public NIST
  standard with no license restricting implementation of its algorithms;
  this entry records the transcription for the same attribution
  discipline this project applies to every other source it ports from.

