NIST CAVP SHAVS test vectors
https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/shs/shabytetestvectors.zip

  tests/vectors/ vendors the NIST Cryptographic Algorithm Validation
  Program's SHAVS (Secure Hash Algorithm Validation System) known-answer
  and Monte Carlo test vectors for SHA-512, verbatim, as downloaded
  2026-08-20 (zip sha256
  929ef80b7b3418aca026643f6f248815913b60e01741a44bba9e118067f4c9b8):
  `SHA512ShortMsg.rsp` (36800 bytes, sha256
  e53a36c03609e5a3e3cc4b6e117a499db7864c23ec825c6cec99503a45f40764),
  `SHA512LongMsg.rsp` (1687845 bytes, sha256
  b1f3f05d5c209777954d49521d7ea1349447c36a0c52849e044bc397a27dd410), and
  `SHA512Monte.rsp` (15215 bytes, sha256
  8ca78659286c2f01667a98fc7accd32fc171ae7b24ac00f1a8ce6b77770247fa). NIST
  publishes these as public-domain test material with no license
  restricting redistribution; they are used only to run sello's own test
  suite (`tests/unit/cavp_vectors.nim`, `tests/unit/test_sha512.nim`) and
  are not part of the built library artifact. `tests/vectors/
  gen_sha512_boundary_vectors.py` additionally generates a small set of
  padding-boundary expected digests via Python's `hashlib.sha512`
  (cross-checked against `openssl dgst -sha512`), an independent
  second-implementation check on lengths (129, 239, 240 bytes) that fall
  outside both the ShortMsg and LongMsg corpora.

