RFC 9496 (H. de Valence, J. Grigg, G. Tankersley, F. Valsorda, I. Lovecruft,
M. Hamburg -- "The ristretto255 and decaf448 Groups")
https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9496

  sello's `src/sello/ristretto.nim` (the ristretto255 prime-order group,
  RFC-004) is a direct transcription of RFC 9496's formulas and constants
  for ristretto255 (decaf448 is out of scope, see the RFC's own Non-goals).
  Field constants (`InvSqrtAMinusD`, `OneMinusDSq`, `DMinusOneSq`,
  `SqrtAdMinusOne`) and the Appendix A test vectors (small-multiples
  encodings, invalid-encoding categories, hash-to-group vectors,
  SQRT_RATIO_M1 vectors) are transcribed from the RFC's own published
  bytes/hex, each cross-checked in `tests/unit/test_ristretto.nim` against
  its defining field equation; individual functions carry a "RFC 9496
  SSX.Y" attribution in their doc comments at the point of transcription.

  RFC 9496 is a product of the Internet Research Task Force (IRTF) and is
  subject to the rights, licenses, and restrictions in BCP 78 and BCP 79
  and Section 4.e of the Trust Legal Provisions
  (https://trustee.ietf.org/license-info). Per RFC 9496's own status
  ("Independent Submission," not a Standards Track document, and carrying
  no IPR-restrictive boilerplate beyond the standard IETF Trust terms),
  its text and code excerpts may be reproduced and its algorithms
  implemented without further permission, provided this notice and the
  standard IETF/IRTF disclaimers are preserved. This NOTICE entry serves
  that preservation for sello's own transcription; the RFC's full legal
  provisions apply to the specification text itself, not to this
  independent Nim implementation, which sello licenses under Apache-2.0
  like the rest of this project (see LICENSE).

